{"type":"output_text","text":{"value":"Here’s a practical, step-by-step example of how to use the synchronous Java SDK (`com.azure:azure-ai-agents-persistent`) to:

- create an agent with a function tool,
- create a thread,
- add a message,
- run the agent with tool calling,
- handle and print the outputs, including tool results.

### Maven Dependency
```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>com.azure</groupId>
  <artifactId>azure-ai-agents-persistent</artifactId>
  <version>1.0.0-beta.1</version>
</dependency>
```

---

### Java Example

```java
import com.azure.ai.agents.persistent.*;
import com.azure.identity.DefaultAzureCredentialBuilder;
import com.azure.core.credential.TokenCredential;

// 1. Configure client
String endpoint = System.getenv("PROJECT_ENDPOINT"); // e.g. "https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>"
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredentialBuilder().build();

PersistentAgentsClient client = new PersistentAgentsClientBuilder()
    .endpoint(endpoint)
    .credential(credential)
    .buildClient();

// 2. Create an agent with a function tool
String modelDeploymentName = System.getenv("MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME"); // e.g. gpt-4o-mini
PersistentAgent agent = client.createAgent(
    modelDeploymentName,
    "Function Tool Agent",
    "You are an agent that calls a function tool."
    // Optionally: Provide a tool manifest/config here if available.
);

// 3. Create a conversation thread
PersistentAgentThread thread = client.createThread();

// 4. Add a user message
client.createMessage(thread.getId(), MessageRole.USER, "Call the add_numbers tool with 2 and 3.");

// 5. Start a run on the thread with the agent (tool(s) attached)
ThreadRun run = client.createRun(thread.getId(), agent.getId());

// 6. Poll for completion (synchronously)
while (run.getStatus() == RunStatus.QUEUED || run.getStatus() == RunStatus.IN_PROGRESS) {
    try { Thread.sleep(500); } catch (InterruptedException e) {}
    run = client.getRun(thread.getId(), run.getId());
}

// 7. Inspect outputs including tool results
PagedIterable<PersistentThreadMessage> messages = client.listMessages(thread.getId());
for (PersistentThreadMessage message : messages) {
    System.out.println(message.getRole() + ": " + message.getContent());

    // If the tool was invoked, check for tool outputs (implementation depends on your tool integration)
    if (message.getToolOutputs() != null) {
        message.getToolOutputs().forEach(
            toolOutput -> System.out.println("Tool Output: " + toolOutput.getResult())
        );
    }
}
```

